WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.150
Hugh Jackman is one of Hollywood's biggest
stars today, thanks to his years playing Wolverine

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.720
in the X-Men film franchise, but he wasn't
always a grizzled, adamantium-clawed hero.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.980
Here's how a lanky Australian teen went from
teaching gym class to ripping people to shreds.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.820
Teaching P.E. in England

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.780
Hugh Jackman was eight years old when his
mother left and moved to England.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:25.640
A few years later, his two sisters moved there
as well, leaving Jackman to grow up in Australia

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.720
with his father and two older brothers.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.560
Jackman admitted that the event left him feeling
"volatile", with a lot of pent-up anger, which

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.520
he channeled into sports at the all-boys school
he attended.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.300
After he graduated, Jackman wound up in England
at age 18 and was hired by the prestigious

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.600
Uppingham School in East Midlands as an assistant
housemaster.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.600
While he spent a good deal of his time teaching
physical education and coaching sports teams,

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.660
part of his duties also included tutoring
freshmen in English and drama.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.860
His first leading role

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.520
When Jackman’s gap year in England ended,
he returned to Australia and enrolled in the

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:04.199
University of Technology in Sydney as a journalism
student, a change in course that would soon

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.040
prove short-lived.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.840
During his final year at university, Jackman
needed a few extra credits to graduate.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.380
He wound up enrolling in drama because he'd
heard it was "easy to pass".

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.859
Little did he realize a lead role in his university’s
production of The Memorandum would put him

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.180
on a path to pursuing acting professionally.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:26.179
After he graduated in 1991, he enrolled full-time
at the Actor's Centre in Sydney, because according

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:29.640
to him, he "didn't have the drive" to be a
professional journalist.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.160
Almost an Aussie soap star

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.539
Not long after Jackman signed with power agent
Penny Williams in the early '90s, he was offered

00:01:37.539 --> 00:01:40.460
a role on the popular Australian soap opera
Neighbours.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:45.149
The show's long been a launching pad for many
future stars, including Kylie Minogue, Russell

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:46.840
Crowe and Chris Hemsworth.

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:51.200
It seemed like Jackman's big break had arrived,
but he'd also recently interviewed for the

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.900
Western Australia Academy of Performing Arts'
acting program, leaving him with a dilemma.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:02:00.260
While the promise of a two-year contract on
a major TV show was pretty alluring, Jackman

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:05.500
ultimately turned it down in favor of continuing
his drama education for a further three years.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:09.980
Jackman loved his time at WAAPA, where he
was immersed in all aspects of training from

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.900
9AM to 6PM every day.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.340
Jackman told The Telegraph:

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.000
"We'd do Shakespeare, then circus skills and
singing and dancing.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.980
It is a quality that seems to tap into my
surname, Jack of all trades."

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.480
Making his major debut

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.580
The same night he finished his last performance
at the drama school in 1995, Hugh Jackman

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.880
got a call offering him a role in an Australian
TV crime drama called Corelli.

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:38.019
The show centered on a criminal psychologist
named Louisa Corelli who gets sent to a men's

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:42.489
prison to work with the inmates and winds
up forming a relationship with one: a hardened

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:44.160
criminal named Kevin Jones.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.940
Jackman was cast as Jones opposite established
actress Deborra-Lee Furness, and though the

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.280
series was ultimately a failure, it wound
up changing his life.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.480
Jackman fell in love with Furness, much to
his embarrassment:

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.159
“I said, ‘Aw, I’ve got a crush on you
Deb, I’ll get over it.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:58.800
I’m sorry.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:02:59.320
I’m sorry.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:02:59.960
It’s embarrassing.’

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:00.540
And she goes, ‘Oh.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:01.900
‘Cause I’ve got a crush on you too.’

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.660
And I was like, ‘Right.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:03.360
What?’”

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.760
The couple married a year later in 1996 and
are still going strong.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.980
A West End star

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.840
Thanks to a critically acclaimed performance
in an Aussie production of Sunset Boulevard,

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:19.010
when it came time to cast the new West End
production of the classic musical Oklahoma!,

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:22.260
producers had only one actor in mind for the
role of cowboy Curly.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.799
Despite fumbling the words while singing "Oh
What a Beautiful Mornin'" during his audition,

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.940
producers were completely enamored with Jackman.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.740
Oklahoma! was a big hit in London, transforming
Jackman into an international star.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.359
Reviews of the actor's performance were beyond
glowing, and he received an Olivier nomination

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.920
for Best Actor for his work.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.360
The production was filmed for television and
aired both in the U.K. and the U.S., where

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:48.260
American audiences were introduced to the
charismatic Jackman for the first time.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.299
Joining The X-Men

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.140
Fellow Aussie actor Russell Crowe was on a
hot streak in Hollywood when Bryan Singer

00:03:55.150 --> 00:04:00.190
offered him the role of Wolverine in his upcoming
film adaptation of the hugely popular X-Men.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:04.700
But the actor turned Singer down, having just
finished Academy Award-winning epic Gladiator.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:09.099
Instead, Crowe told Singer to take a look
at his longtime friend Hugh Jackman, who was

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.520
in London doing Oklahoma!

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.000
Jackman's West End show schedule made the
process a little tricky.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:18.630
The actor had to run over between performances
for his initial audition, and the X-Men team

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.520
were a little put off by his appearance.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.259
Jackman told The Evening Standard,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:26.700
"They basically said, 'Interesting, but lose
the perm and the Southern cowboy accent.'"

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.920
But the audition went well enough they wanted
to fly him to America for a second round.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.820
Jackman hesitated due to his commitments to
Oklahoma!

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:38.480
Eventually, they agreed to send him on a Concorde
jet to America, where he impressed producers

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.120
once again.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.340
Six months of radio silence followed.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:46.850
20th Century Fox execs really wanted Scottish
actor Dougray Scott for Wolverine, but the

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.820
actor was in Australia filming scenes for
Mission: Impossible 2.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:54.479
Disaster struck when Scott was injured in
a motorcycle accident while filming, so with

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.340
Scott unable to film and production rolling,
producers had to find someone else quickly.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.360
Jackman was hired last minute, and a superhero
was born.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.920
Roughly two decades later, Jackman has clawed
his way to the top of the Hollywood heap.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.020
Jackman recalls an opening weekend conversation
with his wife, telling her, quote:

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.180
"I think this is going to change everything."

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:14.720
Was he ever right.

